# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Satyanarayana Bonakala et al. (2026). Towards accurate and scalable high-throughput MOF adsorption screening: merging classical force fields and universal machine learned interatomic potentials.
#   Chemical Science. doi:10.1039/d6sc00831c  arXiv:2509.06719v1
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2509.06719v1 (sha256 676ee31a5c52fa26...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 163 (Application/model instance). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
#
# Encoding scope: bibliographic facts only. The paper screens
# metal-organic frameworks for ethylene capture under humid conditions
# with Widom-insertion Monte Carlo, first with the UFF force field and
# then, for 88 candidates, with the pretrained PFP universal MLIP
# (version 1.19.0, with D3 correction, on the Matlantis platform),
# benchmarked against DFT adsorption enthalpies. It trains no model and
# reports no energy, force or stress error. Read from the arXiv preprint
# (v1).

